{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 17, :comments [{:quotes [{:he "ולזבח השלמים בקר שנים", :translit "u-l'zevach ha-sh'lamim bakar sh'nayim", :gloss "and for the sacrifice of peace offerings, cattle two"}], :mechanisms [{:kind :other, :note "Number symbolism: two cattle correspond to Moses and Aaron as agents of reconciliation"}], :frame {:text "Moses and Aaron are identified as peacemakers. Aaron in particular is described as one who pursued peace between people (Pirkei Avot 1:12, based on Malachi 2:6) and between a person and their spouse (Avot D'Rabbi Natan 12:3). Moses is credited with bringing Israel to reconciliation with God at Sinai (Exodus 19–20).", :sources ["Pirkei Avot 1:12" "Avot D'Rabbi Natan 12:3" "Malachi 2:6"]}} {:quotes [{:he "אילים כבשים עתודים", :translit "eylim k'vasim atudim", :gloss "rams lambs goats"}], :mechanisms [{:kind :other, :note "Three species of offering correspond to two triads: priests/Levites/Israelites and Torah/Prophets/Writings"}], :frame {:text "The tripartite division of the Jewish people into priests, Levites, and Israelites is biblical (e.g., Exodus 19:22, Numbers 8). The Tanakh is traditionally divided into three sections: Torah, Prophets, and Writings, as attested in Bava Batra 14b and Ben Sira's prologue.", :sources ["Exodus 19:22" "Bava Batra 14b" "Ben Sira Prologue"]}} {:quotes [{:he "עתודים", :translit "atudim", :gloss "goats"} {:he "אשר התעתדו לגל", :translit "asher hit'atadu la-gal", :gloss "who station themselves at the mound"} {:he "ועתדה בשדה לך", :translit "v'atadah ba-sadeh lakh", :gloss "and she shall station herself in the field for you"} {:he "וקרבנו", :translit "u-korbano", :gloss "and his offering"} {:he "משנה פניו ותשלחהו", :translit "mishneh panav v'tishlahehu", :gloss "He changed his face and sent him away"} {:he "כי עפר אתה ואל עפר תשוב", :translit "ki afar atah v'el afar tashuv", :gloss "for dust you are and to dust you shall return"} {:he "ויתחבא האדם", :translit "va-yit'chabei ha-adam", :gloss "and the man hid"} {:he "ארורה האדמה בעבורך בעצבון תאכלנה", :translit "arurah ha-adamah ba'avurekh b'itzavon tokh'lenah", :gloss "cursed is the ground because of you, in sorrow you shall eat of it"} {:he "וחפרה הלבנה ובושה החמה", :translit "va-chaf'rah ha-l'vanah u-voshah ha-chamah", :gloss "and the moon shall be confounded and the sun ashamed"} {:he "וימנע מרשעים אורם", :translit "va-yimna mi-r'sha'im oram", :gloss "and He withholds from the wicked their light"} {:he "ואוהביו כצאת השמש בגבורתו", :translit "v'ohavav k'tzat ha-shemesh bi-g'vurato", :gloss "and His beloved as the going forth of the sun in his might"} {:he "כי כימי העץ ימי עמי", :translit "ki kimei ha-eitz yimei ami", :gloss "for like the days of a tree shall be the days of my people"} {:he "ואולך אתכם קוממיות", :translit "va-oleikh et'khem kom'miyut", :gloss "and I will lead you upright"} {:he "הגפן תתן פריה והארץ תתן יבולה", :translit "ha-gafen titen piryah v'ha-aretz titen y'vulah", :gloss "the vine shall give its fruit and the earth shall give its yield"} {:he "והיה אור הלבנה כאור החמה ואור החמה יהיה שבעתים", :translit "v'hayah or ha-l'vanah k'or ha-chamah v'or ha-chamah yih'yeh shiv'atayim", :gloss "and the light of the moon shall be as the light of the sun and the light of the sun shall be sevenfold"}], :mechanisms [{:kind :other, :note "Plene spelling of עתודים with vav signals six blessings/attributes"} {:kind :other, :note "Lexical parallel: עתודים from root ע-ת-ד means standing/stationing, supported by two verses"} {:kind :gematria, :a "וקרבנו", :b "ששה דברים"} {:kind :other, :note "Six things lost by Adam restored in messianic era: radiance, lifespan, stature, fruitfulness of earth, luminaries — each with a proof-text of loss and a proof-text of restoration"}], :frame {:text "Six physical blessings were removed from Adam at the time of his sin and are destined to be restored in the messianic era (Bava Batra 58a lists the loss of Adam's radiance, and Eruvin 13b records that Adam's original stature reached from earth to heaven). The restoration of the luminaries is described in Isaiah 30:26, the restoration of longevity in Isaiah 65:22, upright stature in Leviticus 26:13, and the earth's fruitfulness in Zechariah 8:12. Nachshon son of Amminadab is identified in rabbinic tradition as the first to step into the Sea of Reeds (Sotah 37a, Bava Batra 91a), and his descendant David is blessed with six blessings in 1 Chronicles 11:2.", :sources ["Bava Batra 58a" "Eruvin 13b" "Isaiah 30:26" "Isaiah 65:22" "Leviticus 26:13" "Zechariah 8:12" "Sotah 37a" "Bava Batra 91a" "1 Chronicles 11:2"]}}], :arithmetic [{:kind :other, :note "Number symbolism: two cattle correspond to Moses and Aaron as agents of reconciliation", :by :selah, :ran? false} {:kind :other, :note "Three species of offering correspond to two triads: priests/Levites/Israelites and Torah/Prophets/Writings", :by :selah, :ran? false} {:kind :other, :note "Plene spelling of עתודים with vav signals six blessings/attributes", :by :selah, :ran? false} {:kind :other, :note "Lexical parallel: עתודים from root ע-ת-ד means standing/stationing, supported by two verses", :by :selah, :ran? false} {:kind :gematria, :a "וקרבנו", :a-value 364, :b "ששה דברים", :b-value 861, :lens :standard, :by :selah, :equal? false} {:kind :other, :note "Six things lost by Adam restored in messianic era: radiance, lifespan, stature, fruitfulness of earth, luminaries — each with a proof-text of loss and a proof-text of restoration", :by :selah, :ran? false}], :book :numbers, :voice :baal-haturim, :lang :en, :chapter 7, :discipline "bht-chalkboard-v1", :timestamp "2026-07-12T23:27:51.734807328Z", :model "glm-5.2"}